Microsoft Learn: Implement and Manage Azure Policy

Platform: Microsoft Learn
Module: Implement and Manage Azure Policy
Track: AZ-104 Microsoft Azure Administrator
Difficulty: Intermediate
Date: 2026

Objective

Learn how to use Azure Policy to enforce organizational standards, maintain compliance, and govern Azure resources across subscriptions and resource groups.

This module focused on creating, assigning, and managing Azure Policies and Policy Initiatives to ensure Azure resources remain compliant with business, security, and regulatory requirements.

Step 1: Understanding Azure Policy

The module introduced Azure Policy as Azure's governance and compliance service.

Azure Policy allows administrators to:

Create governance rules
Enforce organizational standards
Monitor compliance
Prevent unauthorized configurations
Standardize Azure deployments

Policies are written using JSON and define rules that Azure evaluates against resources.

Key benefits:
Continuous compliance monitoring
Automated governance
Centralized policy management
Reduced configuration drift
Improved security posture

The module emphasized that Azure Policy helps organizations maintain consistent configurations across large Azure environments.

Step 2: Understanding Policy Definitions

The training covered Policy Definitions, which are the individual rules used by Azure Policy.

A policy definition contains:

Conditions
Rules
Effects
Compliance criteria
Example policies:
Require resource tags
Restrict deployment regions
Enforce encryption
Allow only approved VM sizes
Require HTTPS connections
Key concepts learned:
Policies are stored as JSON definitions
Policies evaluate Azure resources continuously
Policies determine whether resources comply with organizational requirements

Policy definitions are the building blocks of Azure governance.

Step 3: Understanding Policy Effects

A major focus of the module was understanding policy effects.

Policy effects determine what happens when a resource meets or violates a policy condition.

Common policy effects:
Effect	Purpose
Deny	Blocks noncompliant resource creation
Audit	Records noncompliance without blocking
Append	Adds required settings during deployment
Modify	Updates resource properties automatically
DeployIfNotExists	Deploys required resources automatically
Disabled	Turns off policy evaluation
Key lessons learned:
Deny prevents violations before they occur
Audit identifies issues without impacting deployments
DeployIfNotExists can automatically remediate missing configurations

The module demonstrated how policy effects support both governance and automation.

Step 4: Assigning Azure Policies

The training covered policy assignments.

A policy assignment determines where a policy is enforced.

Assignment scopes:
Scope	Example
Management Group	Entire organization
Subscription	Single subscription
Resource Group	Specific workload
Resource	Individual resource
Benefits:
Flexible governance
Granular control
Enterprise-wide enforcement
Key concepts learned:
Policies inherit down the Azure hierarchy
Higher-level assignments affect lower-level resources
Governance can be applied at multiple scopes

The module emphasized selecting the appropriate scope for organizational requirements.

Step 5: Understanding Compliance Evaluation

Azure Policy continuously evaluates resources against assigned policies.

Compliance states:
State	Meaning
Compliant	Resource meets policy requirements
Noncompliant	Resource violates policy requirements
Not Applicable	Policy doesn't apply to the resource
Benefits:
Continuous monitoring
Compliance reporting
Governance visibility
Audit readiness

Administrators can review compliance results through the Azure Portal.

Step 6: Understanding Azure Policy Initiatives

The module introduced Azure Policy Initiatives.

An initiative is a collection of related policy definitions grouped together to achieve a common governance goal.

Examples:
Security Baseline Initiative
Regulatory Compliance Initiative
Cost Optimization Initiative
Data Protection Initiative
Benefits:
Centralized management
Simplified policy assignments
Consistent governance enforcement
Easier compliance reporting
Key concepts learned:
Initiatives contain multiple policies
One assignment can enforce many policies
Initiatives simplify large-scale governance

The module emphasized that initiatives help organizations manage compliance more efficiently.

